🟡 **Medium**

**Bare `catch {}` discards all diagnostic information**

This catch block catches every exception and returns `{ checked: false }` with no logging whatsoever. A bug inside the loop body (e.g. a TypeError on `response.data`) will be indistinguishable from a 503 network error in production logs — both result in a silent refusal to retry. Add at minimum a `console.warn` or `console.error` here so unexpected errors are visible.

*Suggested fix:*

```suggestion
  } catch (err) {
    console.warn("findMatchingReview: lookup failed, treating as unverifiable", err);
    return { checked: false };
  }
```
